        "id": "f7a1c2d3e4b50002",
        "type": "comment",
        "z": "f7a1c2d3e4b50001",
        "name": "FRBC quickstart",
        "info": "A heat pump heating a buffer tank, controlled by a CEM with Fill Rate Based Control.\n\n- **s2-rm-config** advertises FILL_RATE_BASED_CONTROL.\n- **s2-frbc-config** holds the system description (heat pump with Off/Heating modes, 0-100 % tank, 5-minute minimum on/off timers) and the tank's leakage.\n- **Buffer simulator** reports the fill level every 10 s and confirms every instruction. Replace it with your real device: send `StorageStatus { fillLevel }` and, once the device switched, wire the `ActuatorInstruction` payload back as `ActuatorConfirmation`.\n\nThe fill level sent at deploy is stored and sent to the CEM as soon as it selects FRBC.",
